#######################################################
##                                                   ##
## README File for generation of file 7 for N in UnN ##
## using LEAPR module of NJOY processing package.    ##
## Included content is for the generation of the     ##
## inelastic part of the S(a,b) published in         ##
## ENDF/B-VIII.beta5. The coherent elastic xsec and  ##
## incoherent elastic xsec both exist in UN. The     ##
## coherent elastic is put in UinUN library, the     ##
## incoherent elastic is put in NinUN library. The   ##
## coherent elastic xsec in UinUN library (MT = 2)   ##
## was generated using an 'in-house' routine [1].    ##
##                                                   ##
## Compare to beta4 release, the incoherent bound    ##
## xsec for N in UN used to calculate the incoherent ##
## elastic xsec is updated. The coherent bound xsec  ##
## of U in UN used to calculate the coherent elastic ##
## xsec is also updated. The alpha, beta grid for    ##
## S(a,b) is updated.                                ##
##                                                   ##
##  1. Y. Zhu, A.I. Hawari, "Implementation of a     ##
##     Generalized Coherent Elastic Scattering       ##
##     Formulation for Thermal Neutron Scattering    ##
##     Analysis," Proceedings of ICNC 2015: 35th     ##
##     International Conference on Nuclear           ##
##     Criticality Safety (2015)                     ##
##                                                   ##
#######################################################
##                                                   ##
## LEIP Laboratories (Sep 17 2017)                   ##
##                                                   ##
#######################################################
	
NOTES:
1) The incoherent nuclear cross section differs from
   the total for N-14; therefore, the bound incoherent
   cross section must be changed manually to 0.5 barn
   in header of MT = 2 to be consistent with the
   published NinUN library.
2) The published ENDF-BVIII library tabulates the
   incoherent elastic cross section on MT = 2 generated
   by the provided input file.
3) Due the incoherent nuclear cross section of N-14,
   the entire cohrenent elastic cross section for UN
   is tabulated on the UinUN library.
4) The incoherent elastic data exceeds the current
   storage capacity of the NJOY99 ACER module. To
   generate ACE files with NJOY99 the storage capacity
   must be increased in the source code.
	
Folder Content
--------------
tsl-NinUN.endf = File 7 in ENDF-6 format published
         in ENDF/B-VIII (MT = 2, MT = 4)

File 7 Library Parameters
-------------------------
MAT = 71
ZA = 171
Temperatures = 296 400 500 600 700 800 1000 1200 K

NJOY Compilation
----------------
The NJOY99 package used in the processing of these
libraries was compiled with ifort from the intel-2015 
composer suite. The upn was version 396.
